<title>GERMANY: Krupp, Thyssen to cooperate - state.</title>
<headline>Krupp, Thyssen to cooperate - state.</headline>
<dateline>GELSENKIRCHEN, Germany 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The premier of the state where Germany's two steel giants, Krupp and Thyssen are based, said on Friday he was sure that the two would find a common business solution through cooperation.</p>
<p>Johannes Rau, premier of North Rhine-Westphalia,  said that merger talks between Fried. Krupp AG Krupp-Hoesch and Thyssen AG were serious. &quot;They have the will to move away from confrontation and will work on a cooperative solution,&quot; he told a coal conference.  </p>
<p>Krupp has suspended a hostile takeover bid for Thyssen and the two have embarked on a week of talks to try and find a mutually acceptable cooperation deal.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
